WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.110
Good morning, John.

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:05.100
I have a kind of remarkable skill that I've
never talked about here on Vlogbrothers.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:09.280
Spent a lifetime time of work to master it,
it requires a truly mesmerizing amount of

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:12.072
muscle control in my mouth and throat and
abdomen.

00:00:12.072 --> 00:00:16.320
It can be beautiful, it can be terrifying,
depending on my mood, and only one out of

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:19.550
every 8.7 million species on earth can do
it.

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:24.270
Possibly the most remarkable thing I am capable
of doing, I am doing right now.

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:25.270
Talking.

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:26.270
WORDS!

00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:28.530
Noises come out of my mouth!

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:30.630
And I direct them at people.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:33.750
And then the people are like "Yeah I'll meet
you at Buffalo Wild Wings at 7."

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:34.750
It's a miracle.

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:38.970
And it's kind of a miracle we don't notice
how remarkable this ability is.

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:41.820
And we have words for everything!

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:44.280
Like, just look around.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:46.579
This is a book, it's called a book.

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:48.140
But there's more words here.

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:51.130
This is paper and this is cardstock.

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:52.940
This is embossed, it's a embossed cover.

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:55.460
This is a spine, there's blurbs on it.

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:56.460
Blurb!

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:57.460
Blurb is a word!

00:00:57.460 --> 00:01:02.540
This is a llama head stitched to the body
of an elephant theres a word for that.

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:05.860
This thing, put it around your neck, theres
a word for it.

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:06.860
Lanyard!

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:07.860
What--who--came--what--why?

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:10.530
We have words for words.

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:12.020
Nouns and verbs and adjectives and adverbs.

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:14.131
And words for words that mean the same things
as other words.

00:01:14.131 --> 00:01:16.700
And words for things that are the opposite
meanings of other words.

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:20.450
We have so many words that there are some
words that mean the opposite of themselves!

00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:25.150
Inflammable means both very easy to catch
on fire and very hard to catch on fire.

00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:28.390
Sanguine means both cheerful and bloodthirsty.

00:01:28.390 --> 00:01:32.189
Good news though, we have a word for when
words mean the opposite of the thing that

00:01:32.189 --> 00:01:33.189
they mean.

00:01:33.189 --> 00:01:36.070
But if we didn't have a word for it, there
would still be a word for it because we have

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:38.090
a word for when there isn’t a word for a
thing.

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:39.640
Yeah, take so time to think about that.

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:42.990
It is so unusual to encounter a situation
in which you don't have a word for a thing

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:46.450
that most people don't even know there is
a word for when the thing doesn't have a word

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:47.450
for it.

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:50.220
We have a word for the best possible word
to use in any given situation which means

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:54.050
that if you need the best possible word to
describe the best possible word, it describes

00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:55.050
itself.

00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:56.280
In fact there are a number of words that describe
themselves.

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:57.939
A noun is a noun.

00:01:57.939 --> 00:01:59.430
'Cutsey' sounds kind of adorable.

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:03.390
'Magniloquent' means grandiose and also sounds
grandiose.

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:07.690
'Polysyllabic' is polysyllabic, 'unhyphenated'
is unhyphenated, and at one point the word

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:09.119
'coined' was coined.

00:02:09.119 --> 00:02:13.190
You will not, probably, be surprised to find
that there is a word for words that describe

00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:14.190
themselves.

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:18.760
And that word is autological and it is also
autological in that it describes itself.

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:19.760
Blbhblbhh!

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:21.200
That's not the hard part though.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:25.770
The hard part is that autological has an antonym
which is heterological, and heterological

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:29.180
doesn't describe itself because it doesn't
describe itself.

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:32.850
But it does describe itself because--so it's
autologic but if it's not autologic, it's

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:36.470
not autological because it's heterological
so if it's hetero--but if it is heterological

00:02:36.470 --> 00:02:37.720
then it is autological.

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:39.600
[groans, burps]

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:48.250
Luckily, we got a word for that too.

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:51.910
Last year, John and I conducted a census of
nerdfighteria because we wanted to know more

00:02:51.910 --> 00:02:55.040
about this community, and we wanted this community
to know more about itself.

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:58.959
Also it helps us decide what to focus our
time on, where we might go on tour, what new

00:02:58.959 --> 00:03:00.580
shows to be thinking about doing.

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:03.670
The general goal of the census is to make
nerdfighteria a better place.

00:03:03.670 --> 00:03:08.440
So if you have time--and it does take some
time, like 10 to 30 minutes, it's not an insignificant

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:12.810
little survey; there are some real questions
on it that we really want you to answer--then

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:15.420
check the link in the description and fill
out the census.

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:17.040
We will be very thankful.

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:18.540
And it will be making this community better!

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:22.230
Also in the doobly-doo there's a link to nerdfighteria.com,
where you can sign up for a weekly newsletter,

00:03:22.230 --> 00:03:25.690
which you should do because it will keep you
informed on all sorts of amazing things going

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:26.690
on in the world.

00:03:26.690 --> 00:03:29.690
And a list of nerdfighter events that are
happening all over the world that YOU can

00:03:29.690 --> 00:03:30.690
participate in.

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:33.590
Thank you all for being a part of this community
and for putting up with me being confused

00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:34.730
about words.

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:37.510
John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

